# vtium holds its VT: the switch away and back, and keys kept from the
# kernel console (vtium/vtium#19). The steps that read the kernel console
# are run from the desktop, with sudo, while vtium keeps VT {vt}.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=vt

title: vtium holds its VT and its keys

step: Switching away and back
do: press Ctrl-Alt-F{desktop}, wait for the desktop, then press
do: Ctrl-Alt-F{vt}.
expect: the desktop at once, and back here this screen drawn whole, as it
expect: was, with no frame of the kernel console in between.

step: Keys reach vtium only
probe: shell
do: at the prompt type: echo vtium-keys-one
do: then Enter, then exit and Enter. Then press Ctrl-Alt-F{desktop}, and in
do: a desktop terminal run: sudo kbd_mode -C /dev/tty{vt}
do: and: sudo cat /dev/vcs{vt} | tr -s ' ' | grep -o vtium-keys-one
do: then come back with Ctrl-Alt-F{vt}.
expect: kbd_mode says neither Unicode, ASCII nor raw (the keyboard is
expect: off), and the grep prints nothing: the kernel console did not see
expect: the keys.
